Clinical Course: The excessive thirst and urination will continue until your blood sugar is formally managed with medication (likely insulin) by the specialist clinic.
SAFETY-NETTING ADVICE

Seek immediate emergency care if you begin vomiting continuously, or if your baby stops moving normally.
PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: Your pregnancy hormones have caused significant insulin resistance, leading to very high blood sugar. This sugar spills into your urine, dragging water with it (causing the thirst and urination) and feeding the yeast infection. We have confirmed your baby's heart rate is perfect and you do not have dangerous acid in your blood (ketones).
Actionable Steps: Drink only plain water tonight. Eat only protein and complex, high-fiber carbohydrates if hungry. You must present to the high-risk maternity clinic first thing tomorrow morning for formal diabetes management.

